  "research_id": "major-bank-digital-transition",
  "title": "How 16 financial giants are going digital",
  "question": "Where is each major incumbent in the transition from research and roadmap to live money, assets, custody, settlement, collateral and publicly demonstrated recovery, including the quiet migration of retirement fund records and operating rails beneath conventional participant interfaces?",
  "bluf": "Sixteen financial giants are connecting new digital ledgers to existing bank systems. Citi, Bank of America, Deutsche Bank and HSBC show the broadest work, but none has proved one joined system working at large scale or through a serious failure.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-10-14T21:02:44-04:00",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "The sixteen-institution matrix and full recertification remain dated October 3, 2026. The October 14 targeted BNY supplement adds the October 13 reported Citadel Securities Treasury settlement-to-repo workflow. It supersedes the missing-named-obligation negative for that route, remains M4 bounded live, and does not recertify other institutions, prove recurring volume or identify the cash rail. The BNY operating-plan supplement checked through October 14 20:26 EDT distinguishes 2027 service aims, SEC eligibility deadlines, CCP functions and separate Fedwire clocks; the broader bank/platform snapshots retain their dates. October 14 20:38 EDT CIL supplement checks lender-side relief, start/end-leg novation, custody-control and token-admission boundaries; it is not a recertification of the full parent study. The 20:47 EDT missing-link check adds a bounded source/access ledger and distinguishes a mirror interface from an operative token and a broader clearing-hours change; no explicit tokenized-CIL join was located. October 14 21:02 EDT AppChain supplement adds the explicit BNY experiment connection and current FAQ's bounded July CCP-margin evidence; general availability, current launch quarter and BNY/CIL production joins remain unproved. Older financial-model and platform snapshots keep their dated boundaries. October 14 Ripple/Evernorth supplement adds named execution partners, the separate BNY reserve and deposit relationships, and the still-unproved AppChain/CIL transaction join; it does not recertify this package as a whole. A 21:27 targeted supplement now verifies current FICC directory membership and audited conventional repo operation; the XRP-secured-credit-to-FICC allocation remains unproved. A 21:45 parent-repo supplement resolves Ripple as cash lender and Prime US as borrower, without identifying the individual clearing route or use of proceeds. The 22:02 KBRA full-report reading adds April-reported BNY/BMO facilities, the planned additional 2026 parent equity, explicit HoldCo structural subordination, current debt-record maturity and the unverified guarantee/covenant gap. Historical balance clocks and forecasts remain separate. October 14 22:13 targeted credit-structure comparison adds Marex, StoneX, Coinbase and JPMorgan selected instruments; it does not recertify every peer, charter, route or current rating.",
  "use_note": "Use the institution-by-institution receipt matrix and keep parent, regulated subsidiary, account claim, authoritative record, network, CSD, custodian, settlement-money issuer and recovery authority separate. A paper, pilot, partnership or tokenized fund record does not establish workplace-plan adoption, recurring scale or direct token value capture.",
